  "created": "2021-08-06T00:49:24.289Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In some cases, it seems that calling SendCustomNetworkEvent(Owner) can result in a NullReferenceError, and the event not being delivered. This NRE is issued on the _recipient_, not the sender (unless they are also the recipient), and does not actually kill the UdonBehaviour in question, but it does swallow the event.\nMy repro world was working during the 2019 open beta period, so this appears to have been a late regression.\nSample stack trace: https://gist.github.com/bdunderscore/ccf788879d3056474184cef40bacb875\nTest world ID: wrld_24ead743-7877-46a0-96ec-24491ad0fc67\nRepro procedure: Walk over to the panel across the room from spawn and hit the big shuffle button.\nExpected behavior: Shuffling should begin\nActual behavior: The shuffle start RPC is lost, and shuffling does not begin.",
